{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-7brty","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)-7czhh","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/init(_:length:helperText:tableName:bundle:isOutlined:status:autofocus:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/body"]},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter"]},{"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/Length","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/Status"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/View-Implementations"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Layouts","text":"Layouts","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component can be rendered as two different layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"outlined","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" layout: A minimalist input with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages, e.g. when inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a header (search field), or in a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not outlined","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (default): An input with a subtle background fill and visible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component provides 3 layouts for the input: 4 boxes, 6 boxes or 8 boxes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A helper text can be used to support text to convey additional information about the input field, such as how it will be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Error status","anchor":"Error-status","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Error status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or expected formatting.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border, error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input (mandatory).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This state helps users quickly identify and correct mistakes by explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The input remains editable, encouraging users to revise their input without starting over.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The error state must be triggered by an explicit validation (submission, API response), and not in real time with each keystroke.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This can occur either because the entered code does not match the expected code, because the user entered an expired or already used code,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or finally if the maximum number of attempts has been exceeded.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Specific-design-guidelines","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Specific design guidelines"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the context of a PIN code input, in addition to the input’s “Error” UI rendering, it is essential to also include an “Alert” component","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(also in its “Error” status) in the interface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Particular-cases","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Particular cases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" component supports autofill feature of values like OTP code."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if the user receives a message with inside a code the system can extract, the keyboard can suggest to the user to fill it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"If the digits fits the component, it will be filled.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"If the digits are longer, they will be truncated.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits are shorter, they will be filled, letting other fields empty."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The copy\/paste feature is also available and has the same behavior."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Technical considerations","anchor":"Technical-considerations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For some cases, on phones screens or with 8 boxes in iPhone, you may need to use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the component and let user move it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScrollView(.horizontal) {","    OUDSPinCodeInput($value,","                     length: .eight,","                     helperText: \"Enter your secret code sent to your phone\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note also the exposed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"value","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will be updated when all digits are written.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","text":"Accessibility considerations","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The content of the fields is vocalized by Voice Over; the placeholders (defined in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not vocalized to let users know what they wrote.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component gets only numeric values, not letters or symbols, only numbers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Depending on the component configuration, autofocus can still be used when the component appears, and focus is moved to the next field as digits are entered.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For example if Voice Over is enavled, the autoficus is disabled.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component and its digit fields are vocalized with internal wording.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When using the error status, provide a clear, concise error message explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(for example: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“The code you entered is invalid. Try again.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use helper text to communicate additional guidance (for example: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“Check the 6‑digit code sent by SMS”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"), and keep this text short so it remains easy to vocalize","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and understand.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Rich-text","text":"Rich text","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No other text styles should be used.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Code-samples","text":"Code samples","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ The value with the code","    @State private var pinCode: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ By default, the PIN code input displays only 6 boxes","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode)","","    \/\/ It can have also up 4 or 8 boxes, with an helper text","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .eight, helperText: \"Enter your 8 secret digits\")","","    \/\/ The component can be used in error contexts","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .six, status: .error(message: \"The OTP code you entered is not correct\"))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Design-documentation","text":"Design documentation","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-pin-code-input","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Themes-rendering","text":"Themes rendering","type":"heading","level":2},{"anchor":"Orange","text":"Orange","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Orange","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Orange-Compact","text":"Orange Compact","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_OrangeCompact","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sosh","text":"Sosh","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Sosh","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Wireframe","text":"Wireframe","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Wireframe","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Version"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.4.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Since"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudspincodeinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"PIN code input is a UI element that allows to capture short, fixed-length numeric codes, typically for authentication or confirmation purposes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as a four, six or eight-digit personal identification number (PIN).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"PIN code input is presented as a series of individual input fields or boxes, each representing a single digit, to enhance readability and encourage accurate input,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while supporting smooth keyboard navigation and secured input masking if needed.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"title":"OUDSPinCodeInput","externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents16OUDSPinCodeInputV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OUDSPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","platforms":[{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"name":"iOS"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}]},"references":{"doc://OUDSComponents/documentation/OUDSComponents/OUDSPinCodeInput/View-Implementations":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"View Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCod